  "aiSummary": "This bill removes a specific property (86 Magellan Drive, identified as Haywood County Parcel 8604-93-8795) from the Town of Waynesville's municipal limits, effective June 30, 2026. The property will no longer be subject to municipal taxes starting July 1, 2026, though any existing tax liens from the town can still be collected.",
  "aiProArguments": "Supporters may argue that deannexation allows property owners to reduce their tax burden by removing themselves from municipal jurisdiction and its associated fees. They may contend that the property owner prefers county-level services over town services, or that the deannexation better reflects the property's actual use and location relative to town services.",
  "aiConArguments": "Opponents may argue that deannexation reduces the town's tax base and revenue needed to maintain municipal services and infrastructure. They may also contend that removing parcels from town limits creates administrative inefficiencies, reduces the town's financial stability, and shifts the burden of services to remaining residents or the county.",
